# State management (current user)

Session and current-user data live in Zustand (`useAuthStore` in `src/store/auth.store.ts`), persisted with MMKV (`src/store/mmkv_config.ts`). Server lists and screen queries stay in React Query (see `api-integration.mdc`). Do not copy GET list payloads into the auth store.

## Where it lives

| Kind of state | Where | Examples |
| ------------- | ----- | -------- |
| Session + current user | `useAuthStore` | `token`, `user`, `referralCode`, `linkedProvider`, onboarding flags |
| In-progress questionnaire | `assessment.store` | answers, pending submission |
| One-off UI (sheet open, selected tab) | Component `useState` or BottomBar context | see `bottombar-sheets.mdc` |
| Remote lists / detail | UI hook + React Query | foods, recipes, notifications |

Do not add a second “user store.” New user fields go on `useAuthStore` (or a derived selector), not a new Zustand file.

`src/store/store.ts` is leftover app boilerplate — do not put user data there.

## How user information is written

The store is updated **from typed API responses**, not from hand-built objects in a screen.

| Event | Call |
| ----- | ---- |
| Login / social login | `applyAuthSessionFromLogin` → `applyLoginResponse` then `syncMeAfterAuth` |
| Verify OTP | `applyVerifyOtpResponse` (then `syncMeAfterAuth` when that flow does) |
| GET `/auth/me` | `syncFromGetMeResponse` — already run inside `useGetMeQuery` when `data` arrives |
| PATCH health profile | `syncFromHealthProfileResponse` from the profile UI hook |
| PATCH link-provider | `syncFromLinkProviderResponse` |
| Logout / 401 session expiry | `clearAuth` |
| Local assessment done (API lag) | `markQuestionnaireCompleted` |

```ts
// ✅ login hook
useAuthStore.getState().applyLoginResponse?.(response);
await syncMeAfterAuth();

// ✅ profile hook after PATCH
syncFromHealthProfileResponse?.(response);

// ❌ screen
useAuthStore.setState({ user: { ...user, firstName: value } });
// ❌ screen copies query.data.user into local useState and treats that as source of truth
```

`useGetMeQuery` is the ongoing refresh: navigators enable it when `token` is set; its `useEffect` pushes `query.data` into the store. After a mutation that changes the user, either call the matching `syncFrom*` with the mutation response **or** `queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ["me"] })` so GET `/me` re-syncs. Do both when the mutation payload is a partial user (login already does GET `/me` via `syncMeAfterAuth`).

Subscription **access** is RevenueCat (`inapp-subscription-paywall.mdc`). `usePurchases` may mirror `isSubscribed` onto the auth store for routing — do not treat that mirror as the IAP source of truth.

## How information is passed (read)

UI and navigators **select** slices. They do not take `user` as a prop from a parent unless the child is a memoized list item that should stay dumb.

```ts
// ✅ subscribe to one field — only this component re-renders
const token = useAuthStore((s) => s.token);
const referralCode = useAuthStore((s) => s.referralCode);
const firstName = useAuthStore((s) => s.user?.["firstName"]);

// ✅ outside React (api.ts, navigationRef, purchase helpers)
const token = useAuthStore.getState().token;

// ❌ pulls the whole store; every auth write re-renders the screen
const auth = useAuthStore();
const { user, token } = useAuthStore();
```

Pass **primitives** into list rows (`name`, `avatarUrl`), not the store or the full `user` object.

Optional-chain `user` (`user?.["email"]`, `user?._id`). Derive display names in the screen/hook; do not duplicate `fullName` into another store field if it can be computed from `user`.

Routing reads `token` / `user` / `isProfileComplete` from the store (`RootNavigator`, `ensureRootRouteForUser`). Do not keep a parallel “isLoggedIn” in React state.

## Hard rules

- Current user is `useAuthStore.user` (+ token and the derived flags on the same store).
- Writes go through `apply*` / `syncFrom*` / `clearAuth`, not ad-hoc `setState` of `user` in a screen.
- Reads use Zustand selectors or `getState()` outside React — never the entire store object.
- React Query owns lists; the auth store owns the session. Invalidate `["me"]` when the server user changed and you do not already have a full user in the mutation response.
- Logout always `clearAuth` (and the existing navigation reset). Do not leave a stale `user` with a null token.
